# Template for secrets/e2e.env. The real file is gitignored, and unlike
# secrets/next.env and secrets/convex.env it is pushed NOWHERE: `pnpm
# secrets:sync` never reads it, so nothing here reaches Vercel or Convex.
# playwright.config.ts loads it into the test process (scripts/e2e-env.mjs).
# A variable already exported in the shell wins over the value here.
#
# Every variable below is read by a spec under e2e/. When one is unset, the
# spec that reads it SKIPS — Playwright reports a skip, not a failure, so the
# suite stays green while the check never runs. README.md, "End-to-end tests",
# has the full table.
#
# WARNING: `next dev` runs against PRODUCTION Convex (one deployment, see
# CLAUDE.md). The three accounts below are therefore real production accounts,
# and these are their real passwords.

# --- Role coverage: e2e/page-visibility.spec.ts -----------------------------
# Read by credentialsFor() in e2e/helpers/auth.ts. Each pair turns on one case
# of "page list follows the page registry visibility filter", which signs in as
# that role and asserts which page links the home page offers. Both halves of a
# pair are required: either one missing skips the case. The guest case needs no
# credentials and is the only one that runs today.

# An account with the default `user` role.
E2E_USER_USERNAME=
E2E_USER_PASSWORD=

# An account with the `admin` role.
E2E_ADMIN_USERNAME=
E2E_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# An account with the `tom` role.
E2E_TOM_USERNAME=
E2E_TOM_PASSWORD=

# --- e2e/auth-flow.spec.ts --------------------------------------------------
# Turns on the single test "sign up, sign out, and sign back in". Compared
# STRICTLY against the string "1": no other value turns it on. Each run creates
# a new production account named e2e<timestamp> that the spec never deletes.
# E2E_AUTH_FLOW=1

# --- e2e/perfume.spec.ts ----------------------------------------------------
# Turns on the "perfume brew — live sync" block (one test, U7/U8), which drives
# two browser contexts against the shared production Convex deployment.
# Compared for TRUTHINESS, not against "1": any non-empty value turns it on,
# including E2E_CONVEX=0. Empty leaves it off. The test also skips on viewports
# narrower than 1024px, so it runs under the chromium project only.
# E2E_CONVEX=1
